WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
-D'Arcy, it's so great
to see you.

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:03.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey.
Holy cow, you just had a baby.

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:04.070 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I just had a baby.

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:06.072
-What do you guys think of that?
-And it is a crazy --

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:07.540 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:08.074 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Crazy thing.

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:10.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we have actually known
each other for a while.

00:00:10.944 --> 00:00:13.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
We -- well, we were
in a wedding together.

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:16.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our friend John Mulaney
and Anna Tendler got married.

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:17.350 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-They did.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:18.918 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And we both gave toasts
at the wedding.

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:22.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, and I don't know if you
can imagine giving a toast

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:24.457
at, like, a stand-up comedian's
wedding.

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:25.458 line:92%
It's full of stand-up comedians.

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:28.895
It's stressful, and I went
first, and I was really nervous,

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:32.732
and you were there, and some
people that I really look up to,

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:36.403 size:78% position:39%
and I did my speech,
and I kind of killed.

00:00:36.403 --> 00:00:38.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You did great.
-I did great.

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:39.139 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Great.

00:00:39.139 --> 00:00:41.574
-And then up next was Seth,
and then you actually killed.

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:44.911 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I had a good toast. Yeah.
-You had a good set.

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:45.445 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.445 --> 00:00:46.513 line:92%
-It was, like, really good.

00:00:46.513 --> 00:00:49.516 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "Oh, that's --
Okay. No, I get it.

00:00:49.516 --> 00:00:51.251 line:92%
That's what it should have been.

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:52.385 line:92%
That's how you do a toast."

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:55.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, you know, I was like
well -- I did --

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:56.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
We did our speeches.
It is what it is.

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:59.426
But then who comes out next was
John Mulaney's dad,

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:02.762
which I actually was like, "Oh,
he shouldn't go after Seth.

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:05.298
They should have had him first.
This is a dad.

00:01:05.298 --> 00:01:08.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's going to do, like,
weird dad things."

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:08.902 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
He truly killed.

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:10.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Murdered.
-Murdered.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.905 line:92%
-Made us all look like lawyers.

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:13.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The worst.
-Yeah.

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:13.873 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:16.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, we were his like --
we opened for him.

00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:17.877 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it was fantastic.
-He was amazing.

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:21.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I want to talk about "Barry,"
which is a fantastic show.

00:01:21.081 --> 00:01:24.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
Bill Hader plays a hitman
in an acting class.

00:01:24.084 --> 00:01:24.584 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Bill Hader.

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:26.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You are in the acting class
with him.

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:28.788 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yes, Bill Hader right there.
There he is.

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:30.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
Little Bill.
-Little Bill.

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:32.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You first met Bill
because you --

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:33.026 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.026 --> 00:01:34.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, there he is.
-Oh, yeah. Little Bill.

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:36.763 size:75% position:38%
-You nannied for him
like 10 years ago.

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:37.297 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I did. Yes.

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:40.233
I was his nanny for their oldest
two daughters,

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:42.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that was
like my full-time job.

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:44.037 line:92%
I was with them every day.

00:01:44.037 --> 00:01:46.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
I still am really close
with them.

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:48.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
I -- The oldest one
in particular

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:50.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
I, like, hung out with
every day.

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:52.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were like best friends.
-Yeah.

00:01:52.979 --> 00:01:54.013 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Like, that happens,

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:57.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we kind of would just talk
like friends would talk,

00:01:57.717 --> 00:02:00.920
and she, I think, maybe took
after me too much or something.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:05.191
I remember one day I was holding
my phone, and I dropped it,

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:07.660
and I just kind of under my
breathe was like, "Oh, damn,"

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:09.696 size:88% position:44%
and she looked up at me,
and she's, by the way,

00:02:09.696 --> 00:02:11.498 size:78% position:39%
she's two years old,
maybe two and a half,

00:02:11.498 --> 00:02:15.435
and she looked up and she goes,
"Oh, [bleep]. You pooped?"

00:02:15.435 --> 00:02:17.270 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:19.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She thought that's what you
were upset about?

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:20.507 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:20.507 --> 00:02:21.407 line:92%
-Yeah, that's a good friend.

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:22.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know.
-That's a good girlfriend.

00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:25.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's a best friend.
She really knows.

00:02:25.078 --> 00:02:26.212 line:92%
-Yeah, 'cause you want the help.

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:27.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
If that happens,
you want help right away.

00:02:27.981 --> 00:02:29.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No judgment.
You just -- She gets it. Yeah.

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:32.685
-Here's my "I'm gonna wrap
my coat around your waist,

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:33.520 line:92%
and we're gonna find somewhere."

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:36.156
-She would do that for me.
-She would do that for you.

00:02:36.156 --> 00:02:37.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
You also play Janet
on "The Good Place,"

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:40.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is a fantastic role.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:46.733
That you have described as Siri
if Siri had a body.

00:02:46.733 --> 00:02:47.467 line:92%
-Yes, which is exactly --

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:49.869 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, she just --
she knows everything.

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:50.837 line:92%
She's got all the answers.

00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:52.972
-Is it so much fun to be playing
that part

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:53.706 size:84% position:42% line:92%
on that wonderful show?

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:58.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is the most fun I've ever
had doing anything ever.

00:02:58.178 --> 00:02:58.912 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-That's pretty good.

00:02:58.912 --> 00:02:59.679 line:92%
-Yeah, so it's the best --

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:01.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's the best job,
and the cast is amazing.

00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:04.250
-And you work with Ted Danson
who is, I know from experience,

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:05.351 line:92%
is the nicest person on Earth.

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:06.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He loves you.
-He's wonderful.

00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:08.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
He plays -- He plays a demon
on this show.

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:10.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Spoiler!
-Yeah, spoiler.

00:03:10.657 --> 00:03:11.224 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Catch up, yeah.

00:03:11.224 --> 00:03:13.293 size:84% position:42%
-It was a first-season,
first-season spoiler.

00:03:13.293 --> 00:03:13.726 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:16.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But he did not play
by spoiler rules.

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:19.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, he didn't. We were
instructed not to tell anyone.

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:21.100 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, don't tell
your husband or wife.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:24.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
Don't tell your family, anyone
what this big twist was,

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:27.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we really stuck to it,
except he did not,

00:03:27.674 --> 00:03:30.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we found out later
that he did not.

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:33.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
Ted would explain the story to
friends or whoever,

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:36.716
and they would be like, "Oh,
cool. Yeah, that sounds cute.

00:03:36.716 --> 00:03:39.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he would be like,
"Oh, that's cute?

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:40.153 size:81% position:41% line:92%
You think that's cute?

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:41.254 line:92%
Let me tell you what's cute."

00:03:41.254 --> 00:03:43.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then he would tell them
the big spoiler

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:44.791 line:92%
'cause he couldn't handle not --

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:48.027
He wanted the reaction of like,
"Wow, this is really worth

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:50.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
coming back to TV for
or whatever."

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:50.830 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:52.465 line:92%
But, obviously, joke's on them?

00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:54.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, joke's on them.
-I don't know.

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:57.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You also --
We did not meet then.

00:03:57.470 --> 00:03:58.004 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I was there.

00:03:58.004 --> 00:04:01.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were an extra on
"Saturday Night Live" in 2005.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:02.242 line:92%
-Okay, yeah, that's true.

00:04:02.242 --> 00:04:04.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So this is --
David Spade is hosting.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:05.078 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, no, yeah.

00:04:05.078 --> 00:04:08.648
-And you were -- you were -- you
played a woman in the audience,

00:04:08.648 --> 00:04:10.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Martha Stewart.
-Yes, I did.

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:12.252
-So there is D'Arcy right there.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.252 --> 00:04:14.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow. And you know what?
I'm really acting my butt off.

00:04:14.754 --> 00:04:17.190
-Yeah, I will say that you were
doing more acting

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:18.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
than certainly anybody else
here.

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:21.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And can I tell you something?
At the time I knew it.

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:22.895 line:92%
I knew I was doing a good job.

00:04:22.895 --> 00:04:23.630 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Because I want to say

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:25.298 align:start size:94% position:6%
you didn't just stay
in that position.

00:04:25.298 --> 00:04:28.301 size:88% position:44%
You went that. You went
praying hands like that.

00:04:28.301 --> 00:04:28.801 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:30.670
-Seth, can I tell you the scene
called for it?

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:32.372
-Yeah.
-So, that's called good acting.

00:04:32.372 --> 00:04:35.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What I think it really called
for was the fist pump.

00:04:35.375 --> 00:04:36.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
Look at you.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.743 --> 00:04:38.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
Fully doing
your paid extra work.

00:04:38.511 --> 00:04:41.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Why? Why did I do that? Why?
-That was great.

00:04:41.047 --> 00:04:43.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you feel like you were
amongst peers

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:45.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you were in the back
with the extras?

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:49.188
-You know, I -- No, I was like,
"I'm not like them."

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:49.722 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.722 --> 00:04:51.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
Extra work is
so weird and strange,

00:04:51.157 --> 00:04:54.827
and a lot of actors have done
it, or, you know, do do it.

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:56.162 line:92%
And it is a weird little world.

00:04:56.162 --> 00:04:58.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, when I was doing extra
work, I was like,

00:04:58.364 --> 00:05:01.734
"Mnh-mnh, this is not for me.
I can't -- I can't do this."

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:04.137 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I did it,
and you see that I did it.

00:05:04.137 --> 00:05:05.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You fully did it.
-I fully did it.

00:05:05.905 --> 00:05:08.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
-My last question for you is
D'Arcy is spelled

00:05:08.608 --> 00:05:11.044 align:start size:94% position:6%
D, apostrophe, arcy.
-Yes.

00:05:11.044 --> 00:05:14.747
-And this was not your --
This was a choice you made.

00:05:14.747 --> 00:05:15.348 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's right.

00:05:15.348 --> 00:05:17.750 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Your parents named you Darcy
no apostrophe.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:19.485 align:start size:94% position:6%
-My parents named me
normal Darcy,

00:05:19.485 --> 00:05:21.054 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then when I was
in junior high,

00:05:21.054 --> 00:05:24.090
I became obsessed with the band
Smashing Pumpkins,

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:24.857 size:78% position:39% line:92%
which many of us did.

00:05:24.857 --> 00:05:26.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure, who wouldn't?
Of course, yeah.

00:05:26.859 --> 00:05:27.927 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Applause ]
-Okay, cool.

00:05:27.927 --> 00:05:31.130 size:84% position:42%
And the bass player was
this very cool chick

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:34.233
named D'Arcy with an apostrophe,
and when I found that out,

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:36.569 size:88% position:44%
I truly just switched it
and never looked back.

00:05:36.569 --> 00:05:38.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like I didn't --
It wasn't a big decision.

00:05:38.838 --> 00:05:39.639 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Did your parents care?

00:05:39.639 --> 00:05:41.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They did.
-They did? Okay, great.

00:05:41.441 --> 00:05:43.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They didn't love it.
-Yeah.

00:05:43.109 --> 00:05:43.810 size:78% position:39% line:92%
And that's fantastic,

00:05:43.810 --> 00:05:46.245
but it just stuck from there,
and you never looked back.

00:05:46.245 --> 00:05:48.281 size:78% position:39%
-I never looked back.
-Well, it's great.

00:05:48.281 --> 00:05:49.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a very cool way
to spell it,

00:05:49.415 --> 00:05:50.616 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I sign off on it.
-Thank you, Seth.

00:05:50.616 --> 00:05:52.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Not that you were waiting
for me to sign off.

00:05:52.118 --> 00:05:53.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I was,
this moment actually.

00:05:53.152 --> 00:05:56.723
-Okay, great. Thank you so much
for being here. D'Arcy Carden.

